a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\"><em>labyrinth library</em></a><em>. </em></p><p><em>you can </em><strong><em>listen to an excerpt</em></strong><em> below ~</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/blood-in-the-mouth-excerpt\" target=\"_blank\">\n    explore this artifact\n  </a>\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong><em>purpose</em></strong><em> — to notice your relationship with pain — and to bring awareness to the different ways in which you hold it, interpret it, and respond to it. to be with your felt sensations of pain, and create spaciousness between the experience of it — and your response.<br /><br /></em><strong><em>guiding question — </em></strong><em>how can you practice presence with pain — by creating space around it, and allowing it to reveal itself to you?</em></p><p><strong><em>astrological season:</em></strong><em> aries</em></p><p><strong><em>trail-marker word:</em></strong><em> aliveness</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong>🦋 explore </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/labyrinth\"><strong>labyrinth library</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"7647c1c1b816098930dc41bc9eb428020fde6ad2406d8e5122a2858aff6a4ad8","category":"Sites"}